Regular expressions with more than 255 capture groups.

libregexp kept a capture index in one byte, in the header and in the
operands of save_start, save_end, save_reset and the back references,
so a pattern with more than 255 groups was a SyntaxError ("too many
captures"). Browsers allow many more. Discord's main script has a
343-group regular expression literal (its CSS chunk loader), so the
whole script failed to parse and the app never started.

Capture indexes are now 16-bit: the header's capture count is a u16
(the header grows from 8 to 10 bytes, the register count moving after
the bytecode length), save_start and save_end take a u16, save_reset
two, and a back reference keeps its one-byte count followed by u16
indexes. The limit is 65535 captures, and at most 255 groups may share
a name a back reference names. lre_byte_swap swaps the new fields, and
the end-anchored scan of patch 0016 reads the wider save operands.
BC_VERSION is unchanged: the embedder keeps no bytecode across builds,
and upstream's tests embed version-29 bytecode.

